<BaseLayout title="Marketplace Licence Terms" description="Draft commercial licence terms for official pH7Builder marketplace products." path="/marketplace/terms/" robots="noindex, follow">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="narrow-shell">
    <p class="eyebrow"><a href="/marketplace/">Official Marketplace</a></p>
    <h1>Simple terms for small products.</h1>
    <p class="lede">These terms are published for review. Checkout remains disabled until the purchase, delivery and legal checks are complete.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section surface"><div class="narrow-shell prose-block">
    <h2>Marketplace product licence</h2>
    <p>A purchase grants the buyer a non-exclusive, non-transferable licence to use the purchased product on one production pH7Builder installation and its directly related staging or development copies.</p>
    <h3>What is permitted</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Install, inspect and modify the product for the licensed installation.</li>
      <li>Keep private backups and staging copies needed to operate that installation.</li>
      <li>Continue using the purchased version after the support period ends.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>What is not permitted</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Redistribute, resell, sublicense or publish the product or a materially equivalent copy.</li>
      <li>Use one purchase for unrelated production installations.</li>
      <li>Remove licence notices or represent the product as an official release after unreviewed changes.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>The open-source core</h3>
    <p>These terms apply only to the purchased marketplace package. They do not change the MIT licence of pH7Builder or the licences of third-party components.</p>
    <h3>Updates and support</h3>
    <p>The product page states its compatibility range and support period. A purchase does not include customisation, managed hosting or unlimited support.</p>
    <p>Mandatory consumer rights continue to apply. These terms are not a waiver of rights that cannot lawfully be excluded.</p>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
